# Python bytecode from the docs/notes generators
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# KiCad editor lock files and autosave/backup snapshots
*.lck
**/*-backups/
~$*

# Rig firmware build output. NOTE: deliberately scoped to the build dir —
# do NOT add a bare `*.bin` here. The hardware repo had one (inherited
# from the MCU projects) and it was silently swallowing roms/*.bin, which
# are the record of what is physically burned into the sockets.
tests/dino_bringup/build/
*.o
*.elf
*.hex
# Same failure class as the *.bin warning above, different extension: the
# FPGA port's memory-model tests (Task 6) need a real, tracked hex fixture
# (one-byte-per-line "%02x", read by ttl_at28c64b.vhd/ttl_at28c256.vhd/
# ttl_mcm60256.vhd's textio loader) -- not a build artifact, and the bare
# `*.hex` above would silently swallow it exactly the way an unscoped
# `*.bin` once swallowed roms/*.bin. Excepted explicitly rather than
# rescoping the rule above, which is genuinely firmware-build-output-only.
!fpga/ttl/test_memory_16.hex

# fpga/gen/'s own default generic values (fpga_gen.py's MEMORY_INSTANCES)
# point at these -- artifacts-of-record like roms/*.bin, not build output:
# a fresh clone with `*.hex` still swallowing them would have dino_core.vhd
# (and microcode.vhd/memory.vhd) elaborate against DEFAULTS that silently
# resolve to nothing (a zero-filled ROM, no loud failure) instead of the
# real burned images. Regenerated by `python3 docs/notes/fpga_gen.py`.
!fpga/sim/hex/*.hex

# (compiled host-test binaries: see tests/dino_bringup/hosttest/.gitignore)

# Obsidian per-machine editor state. The vault config lives at
# docs/.obsidian/ (an earlier entry here pointed at docs/notes/.obsidian/
# and never matched anything). Scoped to the .obsidian/ config dir ONLY —
# Obsidian keeps notes in the vault proper, never inside .obsidian/, so
# this cannot swallow a .md. Do NOT broaden it to the vault directory.
**/.obsidian/

.DS_Store

# Bench capture files. These are SESSION ARTEFACTS, not project record — a
# `git add -A` once swept screenlog.0 into a commit, and a later `git checkout`
# then restored the stale copy over a fresh run (2026-07-30). Findings belong
# in BRINGUP.md and in commit messages, not in a raw serial dump.
screenlog.*
*.log
